# Secrets / environment (never commit)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Belt and braces: the generator was deleted 2026-07-29, but if anyone hand-writes a secrets
# sheet here it must never be committed. .githooks/pre-commit blocks it too.
/CREDENTIALS.local.md

# Per-install artifacts: if its content depends on WHICH establishment is installed, git does not
# track it. The product names no establishment (README, AGENTS.md § What this project is), and the
# only way that claim survives daily use is if provisioning writes nothing tracked. Both of these are
# written on the install host — the site file by scripts/deis.py, the CSS by phase 15 — and both come
# back on the next `make install`. The DEIS register is NOT per-install: it is the public catalogue
# you pick FROM, so `sites/*/` deliberately matches directories only and leaves the CSV tracked.
/sites/*/
/themes/apsconecta/core/css/site.css

# Local data & Docker volumes (synthetic dev data only, never committed)
/data/
*.sqlite3

# apps/ is bind-mounted to custom_apps, so app-STORE apps (groupfolders, office connectors) install
# INTO it — don't commit their code. Only our scaffolding is tracked.
#
# Our own apps stay ignored too, and deliberately: epidemiologia has its OWN repository, so
# committing it here would give the same files two histories (ADR-0003). What this repo carries is
# its RELEASE TARBALL, under provisioning/apps/epidemiologia/, which is what a server installs from.
# On a dev machine this directory is a clone instead, and provisioning leaves it alone.
# So do NOT "fix" this by un-ignoring /apps/epidemiologia — the declaration is OWN_APPS in
# 12-apps.sh, not an entry here.
/apps/*
!/apps/README.md

# Local agent tooling (regenerable, never committed). The OpenSpec CLI writes these from openspec/,
# so they are output, not source — and they are one vendor's file layout, while AGENTS.md is the
# canonical rules file every agent reads. What IS tracked is openspec/ itself: a spec is a shared
# decision, and ADR-0005 already ruled that those do not live in a working tree.
/.claude/
/.agents/

# Python bytecode — themes/apsconecta/tools/ is a one-shot art generator, not a package
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# IDE / OS
*.code-workspace
.DS_Store

# `make install` writes the full provisioning log here.
.install.log

# The basemap archive: ~1 GB of generated data, rebuilt by scripts/refresh-basemap.sh
# (Territorio ADR-0019). The nginx config beside it IS tracked.
/tiles/

# implement-time evidence transcripts — local only, never tracked (the sites-register and lint-sweep gates own these paths)
/sites/*.txt
/derisk-transcripts/
